'''''Scleranthus perennis''''', the '''perennial knawel''',<ref name=BSBI07>{{BSBI 2007 |accessdate=2014-10-17 }}</ref><ref>{{PLANTS|id=SCPE5|taxon=Scleranthus perennis|accessdate=1 February 2016}}</ref> is a [[Perennial plant|perennial]] [[herbaceous]] plant in the family [[Caryophyllaceae]]. It grows on sandy, dry, acidic soils. It can grow up to 15&nbsp;cm high and has white flowers of 2–5&nbsp;mm. The plant used to be economically significant as the major host plant of the [[Polish cochineal]].
